      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MOSS-Image Base with LoRAs\n\nMOSS-Image **Base** (raw pretrain, Apache-2.0) is the checkpoint LoRAs are trained on. Out of the box its anime\noutput is weak and its photoreal decent; character and style LoRAs improve it a lot. Light data filtering lets\nwatermarks, blur and JPEG artefacts leak in, so keep them in the negative prompt.\n\n**Settings**: 50 steps or more, CFG 3 (true CFG; 4-6 for short prompts), euler, simple, 832×1216 (0.25-4 MP, sides\nmultiples of 16). Shift 5 is applied by the model. **Skip Layer Guidance** (layer 22, 0-1) runs the negative pass\nwith layer 22 skipped, the official default. Tags work best in the order Quality → Score → Meta → Year → Character →\nSeries → Artist → General.\n\n**Prompts**: natural language, booru-style tags or a JSON layout (paste it into the prompt; its size must match\nWidth / Height). Put text to render in double quotes; `(word:1.2)` weights are not known to work. CFG 3 suits long\nprompts; raise it toward 6 for short ones.\n\n## Image Bench\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate tab |\n|--------|------|--------------|\n| `ib:cp` | Load Diffusion Model | model list, model exploration |\n| `ib:pp` / `ib:np` | Image Bench Prompt / Negative Prompt | prompts and LoRA list |\n| `ib:smp` | KSampler | seed, steps, CFG scale, sampling method, schedule type |\n| `ib:lora` | Load LoRA (bypassed) | LoRA exploration only |\n\n**LoRAs**: check them in the LoRA list of the Generate tab, or type `<lora:name:weight>` into the prompt; the **Image\nBench Prompt** node applies them. **Load LoRA** stays bypassed; LoRA exploration enables it for its runs and bypasses\nit again. Use the normal LoRA loaders: `Load LoRA (Bypass)` drops the q/k/v adapters of the fused Comfy-Org\ncheckpoints (watch the console for `lora key not loaded`). Keep the text encoder frozen when training.\n\nThe size is that of **Empty Flux 2 Latent**.\n\nMOSS-Image needs a ComfyUI with native support (merged 16 Oct 2026, PR #17095; master after 0.41.x): an older\ninstall fails to load the model. The CLIP loader type must be `moss_image`.\n\n## Model Links\n\n[Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image) also has `*_int8_convrot` diffusion models (5.4 GB,\nfor 16 GB VRAM or less) and the `qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq` text encoder (7.3 GB).\n\n**diffusion_models**: [moss_image_sft_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/diffusion_models/moss_image_sft_bf16.safetensors), [moss_image_base_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/diffusion_models/moss_image_base_bf16.safetensors)\n**text_encoders**: [qwen3.5_9b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3.5_9b_int8_convrot.safetensors) (one file for SFT and Base)\n**vae**: [flux2-vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors) (the FLUX.2 VAE)\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: MOSS-Image Base with LoRAs"
    }
